# Next.js & Frontend Standards

## Architecture & Rendering
- **Server Components First:** Default to React Server Components (RSC). Use `"use client"` only for user interactions, local state (`useState`, `useReducer`), or browser API hooks.
- **Data Fetching:** Fetch database records server-side via Supabase server client or Server Actions. Avoid client-side `useEffect` data fetching loops.
- **Streaming & Fallbacks:** Wrap asynchronous UI components and dynamic lists in `<Suspense fallback={<Skeleton />}>`.

## UI & Styling
- **Shadcn UI:** Prioritize Shadcn UI primitives for all buttons, dialogs, dropdowns, tooltips, and form inputs.
- **Tailwind Utility Classes:** Use standard Tailwind utility classes only. Do not write custom CSS classes or inline `style={{}}` attributes.
- **Lucide Icons:** Use `lucide-react` for all visual icons, indicators, and action triggers.

## TypeScript Standards
- Enforce strict typing with zero usage of `any`.
- Name prop interfaces following the `[ComponentName]Props` convention (e.g., `LinkCardProps`).